# Schema And CRUD Inputs

- Treat `src/models/` as the runtime Mongo schema and `src/validation/v1/` as the public request contract. `src/validation/v1.validation.ts` is only the compatibility barrel; add new Zod logic to the matching `v1/*.validation.ts` module.
- Keep API and Mongo fields in `snake_case`. Translate only at external boundaries such as CRM payloads and Google Sheets projections.

## Core Collections

- `WordpressFormSubmissionReceipt` (`wordpress_form_submission_receipts`) is a durable WordPress form-submission ingress fact (`autoIndex: false`). It is not a Lead and not a Granot Observation Receipt. Immutable after insert: `source_system` (`wordpress`), `submission_key`, `received_at`, `form_path` (`test` on the authorized path). `lead_ref` is write-once `{ model: "FormLead", id }`. `processing_status` is `received` → `lead_created`. Unique `{ submission_key: 1 }`; non-unique partial `{ "lead_ref.id": 1 }`. Indexes are report-first via `pnpm migration:wordpress-form-submission-receipts`; applied on `testvantagemovers` only. Production apply is refused in the CLI. No contact, payload, CRM, or Sheet fields.
- `FormLead` (`form_leads`) is the website form source lead: source/name/zip/move fields, `phone_number`, optional `email`, `ref_no`, `lid`, `quoted`, `cubic_feet`, `duplicate`, `post_to_granot`, `booked`, `cancelled`, `local`, CPL, and `sheet_sync[]`. Additive Job Number (`job_no` / `normalized_job_no`) is distinct from Tracking Reference `ref_no`. Persisted `move_size` is optional; ordinary WordPress/Admin/import Zod still requires it. Additive lifecycle metadata: required `domain_revision` (default `0`), optional `last_change_id` / `last_changed_at`, write-once `change_history_started_at`, immutable server-assigned `ingestion_origin`, immutable ingested contact/move snapshots, and storage-only Granot/provenance/temporal fields. Receiver-agent source enum includes `granot_username_match`; `extension_crm_username_match` remains readable. Public/admin DTOs cannot set those internal fields. Existing canonical adapters stamp `last_change_*` and increment `domain_revision` from an append-only `EntityChange`; `__v` is not the lifecycle contract. Named S08 Form indexes are created only by `pnpm migration:granot-lifecycle:indexes` after a reviewed report; they are non-unique and never a global unique Lead Job index.
- `EntityChange` (`entity_changes`) is append-only mutation evidence. Unique `{ entity.model, entity.id, revision_after }` plus `{ command_execution_id }`, `{ entity.model, entity.id, applied_at: -1 }`, and `{ changed_paths, applied_at: -1 }`. Contact/address/`$deleted` are `reference_only` with no raw values. Application updates/deletes are rejected.
- `CallLead` (`call_leads`) is the phone/Invoca/CRM-enriched source lead: requires either `phone_number` or `job_no`, normalizes phone for matching, stores CRM enrichment fields, `form_fill`, `created_on_unmatched`, booking/cancellation refs, CPL, and `sheet_sync[]`. Required `quoted` defaults to `false`. Same additive revision/history-boundary fields as Form Lead, plus immutable `ingestion_origin`, ingested contact snapshot, and storage-only Granot/convergence fields. RingCentral adoption adds immutable nested `ringcentral.original_caller` evidence; it is distinct from later-mutable top-level contact facts and from the Granot creation snapshot. Nested `ringcentral.ingestion_source` remains transport provenance. Receiver-agent source enum includes `granot_username_match`; `extension_crm_username_match` remains readable. Public/admin DTOs cannot set internal lifecycle metadata. Lead Job Number is not globally unique. Named S08 Call indexes are created only by `pnpm migration:granot-lifecycle:indexes` after a reviewed report; they are non-unique.
- `BookedLead` (`booked_leads`) links back to `lead_ref` plus `lead_model` (`FormLead` or `CallLead`) via `refPath`, stores customer, job/source/merchant/deposit, required `agent_allocations[]`, `total_binder_amount`, threshold flags, cancellation ref, and `sheet_sync[]`. Same additive revision/history-boundary fields. Unique partial `{ normalized_job_no: 1 }` is the one-Booking-per-normalized-Job contract (`booked_lead_normalized_job_no_unique`; deployed name may still be `normalized_job_no_1`).
- `CancelledLead` (`cancelled_leads`) links to `booked_lead`, customer, source `lead_ref`/`lead_model`, cancel/refund fields, and snapshots booking/customer/source values for reporting. Same additive revision/history-boundary fields. Historical collections are not write targets for these fields.
- `Customer` and `Agent` are support collections. Customers are upserted from source leads during booking; agents are resolved from booking form allocation input and snapshot names on bookings.
- `GranotObservationReceipt` (`granot_webhook_receipts`) is the durable credential-redacted envelope. After insert, only `processing.*` may mutate. `processing.*` is the durable work source for claim/drain; queue payloads are `{ receipt_id }` wake-ups only. Declared due/lease indexes already exist on the model. It does not mutate Leads, Bookings, or Cancellations.
- `GranotObservation` (`granot_observations`) is one normalized Granot statement per receipt. It is evidence only. Unique index is `receipt_id`. It does not mutate Leads, Bookings, or Cancellations.
- `DomainCommandExecution` (`domain_command_executions`) is the durable idempotent command result. Origins are `external_sheet_ingestion | vantage_admin | granot_lifecycle | ringcentral`. New rows store nested `result.status: "applied"` plus compatibility top-level `entity_refs` / `warnings`. Unique indexes remain `(origin, idempotency_key)` and `command_id`. Legacy rows without `result` are read by derivation and are not rewritten. The executor owns the transaction; Sheet Sync does not persist commands.
- `SynchronizationDecision` (`synchronization_decisions`) is one immutable row per observation/attempt. Unique index is `{ observation_id, attempt }`. Additive `source_policy` preserves the exact reviewed Granot source/disposition/version even when Referral intentionally has no Lead Source Scope. The processor stamps `processing.latest_decision_id` on the source receipt; it does not claim or drain the receipt.
- `GranotLifecycleActivation` (`granot_lifecycle_activations`) is write-once. Unique index is `{ key: 1 }`. No API delete/edit exists.
- `GranotRecordLink` (`granot_record_links`) is the current job-level link aggregate. Unique partial index is `{ provider, normalized_job_no }` where `state:"active"`. Historical shadow may create a lead-less job-level row. Authorized create/sync/confirm may attach `lead_ref`, `source_scope`, and later `booking_ref`.
- `GranotBookingReconciliationCase` (`granot_booking_reconciliation_cases`) is append-only Owner work for Priority `5` / Booked evidence, including `create_referral_booking` without Source Scope or Lead suggestion. Unique indexes are open `{normalized_job_no, action_kind}` (partial on `state:"open"`) and `{normalized_job_no, action_kind, sequence_number}`. It is not a Booking.
- `GranotCrmSource` (`granot_crm_sources`) remains the operational CSV catalog and is now also the only semantic Granot source Registry. Additive lifecycle fields default to `lifecycle_enabled=false`, `lifecycle_disposition=deferred`, `lead_created_policy=observation_only`, and empty routes. Optional `outbound_sms` defaults off / `not_attested` and is backfilled; it never enables a send by itself. `create_if_missing` does not send texts. Do not repurpose legacy string `source_company` as `lead_source_company`. The unique `{ normalized_granot_label: 1 }` index is declared but not production-applied until Unit 06 collision inventory is zero.
- `LeadMessage` (`lead_messages`) is the durable outbound SMS record. Public-form confirmations still store `form_lead`. Additive `lead_ref` (`{ model: "FormLead" | "CallLead", id }`) is the polymorphic Lead pointer. Phase-1 backfill (`pnpm migration:lead-message-lead-ref`) copies `form_lead` onto `lead_ref` with `origin: public_form` and does not relax `form_lead`. Production `vantagemovers` updated 1314 messages. // pragma: allowlist secret

## Input Contracts

- Routes in `src/routes/v1.routes.ts` parse every create/update/search body with strict Zod schemas before calling services. Update schemas are partial but require at least one field.
- Form lead create accepts landing-page fields plus `crm_company_label` and `post_to_granot`; duplicate detection can force `post_to_granot=false`. Optional `wordpress_submission_key` (trim, 8–128) is stripped before Form Lead persist and is never inferred. Patch form leads for extension-owned updates such as `quoted` and `cubic_feet`.
- Call lead create accepts sparse call data but must include `phone_number` or `job_no`. Enrichment endpoints accept batches of CRM rows (`row_id`, job/customer/phone/email/zips/est_cf).
- Booking create can use direct `lead_ref`/`lead_model` plus `agent_allocations`, or `/booked-leads/from-source` with `lead_type` (`FormLead` uses `form_lead_id`; `CallLead` uses `call_job_no` or `call_phone_number`).
- Cancellation create requires either `booked_lead` or `lead_id`; if both are present, services enforce that they point to the same booking/source lead chain.
- Owner requeue `POST /api/v1/admin/granot-lifecycle/receipts/:id/requeue` body is `{ reason }` (trim 10–500, unknown keys rejected). Only `dead_letter` is eligible.
- Owner Booking commands require exactly one `Idempotency-Key` header. Confirm body is `{ expected_case_revision, selected_lead?, official_booking_details, out_of_scope_override_reason? }`. `selected_lead` is optional; unknown keys still reject. Referral create body is exactly `{ expected_case_revision, official_booking_details }` with no Lead/Job/contact/source fields. Update body is `{ expected_case_revision, expected_booking_revision, official_booking_details }`. No Action body is `{ expected_case_revision, reason_code?, reason_text? }`. Official details use calendar-valid `YYYY-MM-DD`, `primary_agent_id`, optional `secondary_agent_id` (must differ), `total_binder_amount`, Deposit, and Merchant. Per-agent `agent_allocations[]` is rejected; the server derives stored allocations via even-cent split.
- Granot lifecycle case/Job/Lead reads use strict cursor/filter schemas in `v1/granotLifecycle.validation.ts`. Case list defaults to merged open Booking/Release rows ordered by newest evidence; `kind=release` uses projection mode `release`. Timeline limit is 100 (max 200); candidate browsing is Booking-only, defaults to Source Scope, and is Owner-only. Unknown keys and malformed IDs/dates/ranges/cursors fail with `GRANOT_VALIDATION_FAILED`.

## Change Guidance

- When changing persisted fields, update the model, validation schema, service mirror logic, sheet projections/headers, and any docs or form scripts that submit the field.
- Do not bypass service helpers for source-company parsing, phone normalization, local/CPL derivation, agent allocation resolution, duplicate/form-fill checks, or sheet-sync scheduling.
